  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos. ARCH-4 says changes to the event must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but I can't see those consumers. A deployed consumer that still reads the field would break if it disappeared.\n\nHere are the options:\n1. **Deprecate first (my suggestion).**\n   - Mark `channel` as deprecated in `src/core/events.ts`.\n   - Make it optional in `POST /orders` so clients can stop sending it.\n   - Keep populating it on the event, with a default if the order has none.\n   - Remove it once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't read it.\n2. **Remove it now.** I'd do this if you can confirm both teams have signed off, or that ARCH-4 doesn't apply here. I'd then drop it from the event, `Order`/`NewOrder`, validation, request parsing, the `CHANNELS` type, the tests, and the examples in README.md and CLAUDE.md.\n3. **Remove it from the internal order model only.** The event would still carry `channel`, so that doesn't fully do what you asked. It also needs a source for the value, so it's awkward.\n\nWhich one do you want?",
